often made. Uncle's steaming pork sat in the middle of the table,

45
00:03:37.688 --> 00:03:41.416
smelling delicious. The sound of drums filled the night and guests hula

46
00:03:41.417 --> 00:03:45.714
danced. Auntie danced nearby as Grandfather plucked the strings of his

47
00:03:45.715 --> 00:03:52.391
ukulele. "Portuguese immigrants, like my family, brought the instrument to Hawaii in 1879," he

48
00:03:52.392 --> 00:04:00.927
explained. "The Hawaiians named it ukulele, which means 'jumping flea,' because of the way the musician's fingers jumped across the

49
00:04:00.928 --> 00:04:05.335
strings." "Traditional hula only used drums," Auntie

50
00:04:05.336 --> 00:04:09.003
said. "Other instruments, like the ukulele, were added

51
00:04:09.004 --> 00:04:13.425
later. Originally, the dances told stories about the ancient

52
00:04:13.426 --> 00:04:20.428
gods." Kaycee joined Auntie, swaying her hips and following the motions of Auntie's arms and

53
00:04:20.429 --> 00:04:22.574
hands. "Hey," she said

54
